# Frontend (Jinja templates)

- Use semantic HTML (`main`, `header`, `section`, `footer`).
- No API calls or business logic in templates — only display `weather` fields passed from routes.
- Error UI lives in `_error.html`; keep messaging user-friendly.
- Link static assets with `url_for('static', filename='...')`.
- Prefer accessible labels on form inputs; include attribution link to Open-Meteo in the footer.
- `static/app.js` may update the DOM and use `localStorage`; never call Open-Meteo from the browser.
